data = ["Once there was a shepherd in a village. He used to take his flock of sheep to the nearby forests for grazing. After a few days, he found his job boring and thought of making it more fun.One fine day, while the sheep were grazing, he gave a loud cry, “Wolf!, Wolf! Somebody, please help. A wolf is taking away my lamb.” The farmers working closeby heard the cry and came running for its rescue.Upon reaching, they could not find any wolves. The boy jokingly said that he lied just for fun. After realising this, people left the place. But the boy kept on playing similar tricks frequently.One day the boy really cried for help when the wolf arrived and attacked the flock. But this time, nobody believed him and thought he was again trying to fool them.Moral: Once you are called a liar, no one will believe you even if you say the truth. Lying can lead to losing people’s trust when you need it most. On a sunny day, a crow feels thirsty and goes in search of water near the forest. It flew across the jungle but was still not able to find a water source anywhere. Suddenly it’s eyes fell on a jug of water.When it reached the jug to drink, it noticed that the water level was too low and the opening of the jug was narrow. The crow’s beak could not reach it. Eventually, it came up with an idea. The crow started collecting pebbles around the jug and dropped them into the water.Slowly, the water level started rising. Finally, the crow quenched its thirst.Moral: Where there is a will, there is a way. It teaches the morals of perseverance and problem solving. "]

